      "NAME LIKELY CONFLATES TWO PEOPLE (research 2026-07-03, unresolved): period Jamestown sources (WikiTree Biggs-87; the 1624/25 Virginia Muster; multiple Biggs-family genealogies) show two separate women associated with a Richard Biggs of early Virginia — an \"Anne Juxon,\" and a wife named \"Sarah\" (age 35 in the 1624 muster, immigrated May 1618 on the Marygold). This record's compound name \"Sarah Anne Juxon Marshe\" appears to string at least two distinct identities together, plus an unexplained \"Marshe.\" It's also internally inconsistent: a 1581 birth year would make her 43 at the 1624 muster, not 35. Treat the identity as unresolved rather than one documented person pending a primary muster/parish-record check."
